  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A=\\{\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\delta \\}.$ \n\n$$\nR=\\{(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\alpha ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\delta ),(\\delta ,\\beta )\\}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}\n$\\in R$ and \n{{field-2}}\n$\\in R,$ but \n{{field-3}}\n$\\notin R,$ the relation is\n{{field-4}}.",
